Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:06.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}How robust can any classifier possibly be against an adversary that perturbs inputs at test time?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.59,0:00:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper answers that question for the multi-class setting.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.42,0:00:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors derive achievable information-theoretic lower bounds on the 0-1 loss of the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.88,0:00:19.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}best possible classifier under a test-time attacker,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.14,0:00:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}for any discrete dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.71,0:00:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Their framework builds a conflict hypergraph from the data and the attacker's constraints,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.36,0:00:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then solves a linear program whose optimum is the lowest loss any classifier can attain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.89,0:00:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because the exact problem is often too large to solve,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.28,0:00:39.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they introduce efficient bounds that pin down the range of the optimal loss,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.05,0:00:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and use them to reveal a striking gap between today's adversarially trained models and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.45,0:00:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}what is theoretically achievable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.82,0:00:53.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Determining whether a classifier is truly robust to adversarial examples requires knowing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.64,0:00:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the best that is even possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.67,0:01:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For binary classification, prior work characterized this optimal robust loss,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.70,0:01:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving a reference point to measure progress against.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.17,0:01:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But real problems have many classes, and the multi-class case was left open.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.13,0:01:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}There was no way to compute the lowest 0-1 loss achievable by any classifier against a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.76,0:01:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}test-time attacker on a multi-class dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.63,0:01:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so practitioners had no way to know how far current defenses sit from the theoretical limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.95,0:01:29.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Comparing the robustness of the best possible classifier to what state-of-the-art training
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.51,0:01:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}achieves is a powerful diagnostic.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.61,0:01:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It tells you whether the bottleneck is your training method or a fundamental limit of the data and threat model.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.53,0:01:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Past work delivered this only for two classes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.37,0:01:46.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Moving to many classes is not a trivial extension: with three or more classes,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.19,0:01:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}examples can interact in higher-order ways that binary analysis simply cannot capture,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.51,0:01:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and these interactions can change what optimal robustness looks like.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.07,0:01:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes three contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.96,0:02:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.85,0:02:07.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it generalizes the conflict-graph framework from binary to multi-class classification,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.74,0:02:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing the optimal 0-1 loss is the solution of a linear program built on a conflict hypergraph.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.63,0:02:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, because that exact program can become computationally prohibitive,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.52,0:02:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it develops several more efficient bounds, both lower and upper,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.41,0:02:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that bracket the range in which the true optimal loss must lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.30,0:02:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, it delivers an extensive empirical study,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.19,0:02:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving the first analysis of the gap to optimal robustness for classifiers in the multi-class
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.08,0:02:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}setting on benchmark datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.27,0:02:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The core idea is to represent the classification problem as a conflict hypergraph.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.48,0:02:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each vertex is a data point,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.25,0:02:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a set of points forms a hyperedge when they belong to different classes yet share
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.65,0:02:49.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}overlapping adversarial neighborhoods,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.06,0:02:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}meaning an attacker could push any of them to the same confusing input.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.57,0:03:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The optimal 0-1 loss then becomes a linear program: maximize the probability mass of correctly
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.54,0:03:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}classified points subject to constraints encoded by the hypergraph's incidence matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.00,0:03:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The dual program is a fractional covering of vertices by hyperedges,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.32,0:03:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it directly yields the optimal adversarial strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.87,0:03:17.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because computing all hyperedges up to degree ten is infeasible,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.93,0:03:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors truncate the hypergraph to lower degrees for tractable lower bounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.01,0:03:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}aggregate binary one-versus-one losses for an even cheaper bound,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.14,0:03:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and apply a generalized Caro-Wei bound for a matching upper bound.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:36.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The experiments use two standard vision benchmarks, MNIST and CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.36,0:03:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}under an L-two constrained attacker evaluated across a sweep of perturbation budgets.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.02,0:03:47.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For the 3-class studies they take one thousand samples per class, using digits one,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.55,0:03:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}four, and seven for MNIST and the plane, bird, and ship classes for CIFAR-10.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.68,0:03:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They also compute bounds for the full 10-class problem on the complete training sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.34,0:04:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}As reference defenses, they train classifiers with TRADES adversarial training,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.60,0:04:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a small convolutional network for MNIST and a wide residual network for CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.00,0:04:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and evaluate them with the strong APGD attack from AutoAttack.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.43,0:04:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline finding is a large, previously unquantified gap.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.43,0:04:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Adversarially trained classifiers perform far worse than the theoretical optimum,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.75,0:04:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and this gap is much wider than what prior work observed for binary classification.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.20,0:04:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On 3-class CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.52,0:04:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}TRADES adversarial training cannot achieve a loss much better than 0.6 at a perturbation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.29,0:04:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}strength where the optimal achievable loss is essentially zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.43,0:04:40.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the 10-class setting,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.00,0:04:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the efficient lower and upper bounds sandwich the optimal loss tightly for the budgets used in practice,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.83,0:04:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the gap is not an artifact of loose bounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.85,0:04:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This suggests current robust training struggles far more as the number of classes grows.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.93,0:05:00.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A key ablation examines how much the higher-order hyperedges actually matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.90,0:05:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Surprisingly,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.87,0:05:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at small perturbation budgets the lower bound computed with only edges is nearly identical
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.84,0:05:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}to bounds that add degree-three and degree-four hyperedges,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.81,0:05:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}even though the graph contains millions of these higher-order structures.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.78,0:05:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For CIFAR-10 at budget three,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.76,0:05:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}there are roughly three million degree-three and ten million degree-four hyperedges,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.73,0:05:28.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet they have no impact on the computed bound.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.70,0:05:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This means edge-only bounds are both cheap and accurate in the practical regime.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.67,0:05:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The aggregated binary bound is the fastest to compute but much looser,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.64,0:05:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and scaling up model architecture yields only minor gains at low budgets.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.91,0:05:45.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The numbers make the gap concrete.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.11,0:05:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On 3-class CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.31,0:05:53.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}adversarial training plateaus near 0.6 loss at a budget where the optimal loss is essentially zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.51,0:05:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}State-of-the-art certifiably robust models fare no better against the optimum: the best
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.72,0:06:01.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}MNIST model has 0-1 loss of 0.27 at budget one-point-five-two and 0.44 at budget two,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.92,0:06:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while the achievable optimal lower bound is zero in both cases.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.12,0:06:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.32,0:06:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the best certified model reaches 0.6 loss at budget one and 0.8 at budget two,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.52,0:06:18.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}again against an optimal lower bound of zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.72,0:06:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And on the structural side, millions of higher-degree hyperedges,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.93,0:06:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}three million of degree three and ten million of degree four at budget three,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.13,0:06:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}leave the bound completely unchanged.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.63,0:06:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is that multi-class robust classification has a large and now-measurable
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.83,0:06:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gap between what current defenses achieve and what is theoretically possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.54,0:06:44.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a gap that is far worse than in the binary case.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.48,0:06:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper's conflict-hypergraph framework computes the optimal 0-1 loss as a linear program,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.11,0:06:57.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and its efficient truncated bounds pin that optimum down tightly using only edges in the practical low-budget regime.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.27,0:07:03.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This gives practitioners a fast diagnostic tool to see how much robustness is still on the table,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.20,0:07:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it points future research toward closing the gap rather than endlessly iterating attacks and defenses.
